     1,
     "Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I am new at statistics and lavaan, and have been runing into the following error: <span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px\">I have been getting the lavaan ERROR: at least one variance in the sample covariance matrix is (near) zero or negative.</span></div><div><br></div><div>When I check the covariance matrix, I don&#39;t see any number that is near zero or negative.  What am I missing? I am pasting two of the covariances matrices below. From EFA and reliability results, I assume the first one will lead to a poor fit - but wouldn&#39;t CFA run anyway? The second matrix relates to what seems to be a strong scale, according to EFA and reliability. </div><div><br></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(148,148,148)\"># A tibble: 5 × 5</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\r\n     v1    v2    v3    v4    v5\r\n  </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;font-style:italic;color:rgb(148,148,148)\">&lt;dbl&gt;</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\"> </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;font-style:italic;color:rgb(148,148,148)\">&lt;dbl&gt;</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\"> </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;font-style:italic;color:rgb(148,148,148)\">&lt;dbl&gt;</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\"> </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;fon