    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">If you can print out the covariance matrix so it looks like a matrix, it would be easier to diagnose.<div><br></div><div>If you write out the code so that it would be reproducible, it would be even easier.   There are instructions here: <a href=\"https://www.r-bloggers.com/2011/01/three-tips-for-posting-good-questions-to-r-help-and-stack-overflow/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.r-bloggers.com/2011/01/three-tips-for-posting-good-questions-to-r-help-and-stack-overflow/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414983221000&amp;usg=AOvVaw03Htvcl1wi_j19TSa5-6MW\">https://www.r-bloggers.com/2011/01/three-tips-for-posting-good-questions-to-r-help-and-stack-overflow/</a></div><div><br></div><div>Jeremy</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
