    [
     1,
     "<div>Is dim_pb3 a data frame or a data-frame-like object, e.g., a tibble?</div><div><br></div><div>It seems that sample.cov does not support a covariance matrix in the form of a data frame:</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\">``` r<br>library(lavaan)<br>#&gt; This is lavaan 0.6-17<br>#&gt; lavaan is FREE software! Please report any bugs.<br>HS.model &lt;- &#39; visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3<br>              textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6<br>              speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9 &#39;<br><br>dat_cov &lt;- cov(HolzingerSwineford1939[, paste0(&quot;x&quot;,1:9)])<br>fit1 &lt;- cfa(HS.model, sample.cov = dat_cov, sample.nobs = 300)<br><br># Convert the covariance matrix to a data frame<br>dat_cov_as_df &lt;- as.data.frame(dat_cov)<br>fit2 &lt;- cfa(HS.model, sample.cov = dat_cov_as_df, sample.nobs = 300)<br>#&gt; Error in lavData(data = data, group = group, cluster = cluster, ov.names = OV.NAMES, : lavaan ERROR: at least one variance in the sample covariance matrix is (near) zero or negative.<br>```<br></font><br>&lt;sup&gt;Created on 2024-02-14 with [reprex v2.1.0](<a href=\"https://reprex.tidyverse.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://reprex.tidyverse.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414983230000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1aQ1sbE71nlv-jLeEfv0rd\">https://reprex.tidyverse.org</a>)&lt;/sup&gt;<br></div><div><br></div><div>The example above had two errors and so may be different from your case, but it does the have the error about variance. You can try converting dim_pb3 to a matrix by as.matrix() and see whether you still have the error message.</div><div><br></div><div>By the way, you mentioned that you are &quot;working with the pooled covariance matrix after multiple imputation using mice.&quot; Just curious. Should cfai.mi() from semTools be used in this case?</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://rdrr.io/cran/semTools/man/runMI.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/cran/semTools/man/runMI.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414983230000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0FH-ii5huLfVI0ySsvFldC\">https://rdrr.io/cran/semTools/man/runMI.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>-- Shu Fai</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wednesday, February 14, 2024 at 12:30:30 AM UTC+8 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">kikabr...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I am new at statistics and lavaan, and have been runing into the following error: <span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px\">I have been getting the lavaan ERROR: at least one variance in the sample covariance matrix is (near) zero or negative.</span></div><div><br></div><div>When I check the covariance matrix, I don&#39;t see any number that is near zero or negative.  What am I missing? I am pasting two of the covariances matrices below. From EFA and reliability results, I assume the first one will lead to a poor fit - but wouldn&#39;t CFA run anyway? The second matrix relates to what seems to be a strong scale, according to EFA and reliability. </div><div><br></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(148,148,148)\"># A tibble: 5 × 5</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\r\n     v1    v2    v3    v4    v5\r\n  </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;font-style:italic;color:rgb(148,148,148)\">&lt;dbl&gt;</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\"> </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;font-style:italic;color:rgb(148,148,148)\">&lt;dbl&gt;</span><span style=\"outline:none;borde